TEXT 0 -480 Left 2 ;Lab E part 2 - System D woofer (Scan-Speak 26W/8534G00) in its 88.1 L box, vent PLUGGED.  Parameters: Scan-Speak data sheet.
TEXT 0 -448 Left 2 ;IMPEDANCE analogy in all three domains: electrical V = voltage, I = current | mechanical V = force, I = velocity | acoustical V = pressure, I = volume velocity
TEXT 0 -400 Left 2 !.param Vg=2.83 r=1.0 Wb=0.435 Re=5.7 Le=0.00096 Bl=10.1 Mmd=0.046724 Rms=0.8 Cms=0.00095 Sd=0.035
TEXT 0 -368 Left 2 !.param MA1=3.0823 RA1=5207.1 RA2=11808 CA1=4.9246e-08 CAB=6.2104e-07 rho=1.2041
TEXT 0 352 Left 2 ;acoustic load: box compliance C_AB (rear, vent plugged) in series with the front radiation impedance Z_ar (baffled piston)
TEXT 0 384 Left 2 ;V(pD) = (Z_ar + 1/(s C_AB)) U drives the reaction force;  V(pF) = Z_ar U is the pressure on the front of the cone
TEXT 1344 304 Left 2 ;outputs (plot in dB, they read directly as dB SPL at distance r for e_g = Vg)
TEXT 0 880 Left 2 !.param wst={sqrt(2)*2*pi*115/Wb} k2pi={rho*Sd/(2*pi*r*20u)}
TEXT 0 912 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 10 20k
TEXT 0 960 Left 2 ;SPL2pi: p = j*w*rho*Sd*u/(2 pi r) (half space, infinite baffle, = the data sheet condition).  SPL4pi = 6 dB lower (full space, what a small box does at low f).
TEXT 0 992 Left 2 ;SPLbs: SPL2pi x (s + wst/2)/(s + wst): first-order baffle step, -3 dB at 115/Wb Hz. Rule of thumb only; the measured curve adds edge-diffraction ripples on top.
TEXT 0 1040 Left 2 ;check: |Z_E| peak 127 ohm (radiation resistance adds to R_MS) at f_c = 39.0 Hz (Lab D measured 123 ohm at 42.0 Hz), Q_tc = 0.66;  mid-band V(SPL2pi) = 90.4 dB at 2.83 V, 1 m (data sheet 89 dB);  ka = 1 at 518 Hz
TEXT 0 1072 Left 2 ;In the chamber ignore everything below ~125 Hz.  Not in this model: off-axis beaming (2 J1(ka sin th)/(ka sin th)) and the diffraction ripples (diffrac.m).
